  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional Capacity Development Project by the Refugee Consortium of Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching objective of the Inclusive Refugee Response Programme 2023 &#x2013; 2026 is to enhance self-reliance, resilience and long-term stability for refugees and host communities in especially Turkana County by supporting Kenya&#x2019;s national and locally led development efforts to improve access to inclusive basic social services, thereby contributing to a reduction of inequality and poverty. 

Building on Refugee Consortium of Kenya (RCK) core strength which is legal policy advocacy and influencing through high level  engagements, capacity building and technical assistance, the Royal Danish Embassy in Nairobi will engage RCK in the implementation of the project. RCK will build on previous work to advocate for recognition of refugee identification services especially in the access services, and will work closely with county and national government to facilitate access to health, education, and health services for refugees as outlined in the Constitution of Kenya.</narrative>
  </description>
